// FIELD SERVICE — SLAP HAPPY — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// FIELD SERVICE as future funk — a game alternate of plumber, selectable from the dev
// menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the live song.
// 
// A little swing on the sixteenths, four on the floor with disco open hats and
// congas, a slap bass (thumb on one lane, octave pops on another), a Rhodes comping
// ninth chords, and the hook SUNG — vocal chops in the verse, a 70s voice box in the
// chorus with the chops a third under it (exactly the line plumber.js's own leadHarm
// plays). Strings and brass for the lift. The harmony is the tune's own, dressed:
// | Am9 Fmaj9 | Cmaj9 G13 | for the A phrase.
// 
//   1–4    intro — Rhodes, hats, a sung answer (the cabinet-screen loop)
//   5–12   verse — the band in; vocal chops sing A A B B
//   13–16  pre — Dm9 Em7 Fmaj9 G13 climbing, strings, riser
//   17–32  chorus — voice box over chops, brass stabs: A A B B A A C C
//   33–40  breakdown — bass, congas, Rhodes; ii-V-I in C, then E7 home
//   41–44  pre again
//   45–60  chorus two — strings on the harmony line
//   61–64  outro — Rhodes and chops; the loop returns to bar 5
// 
// 64 bars at 116, swing 56. Written by work/local/_fs-remix-slap-happy.mjs
// through work/local/_fs-remix-lib.mjs; re-running it rewrites this file.
//
